{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "checkmk-raw",
  "description": "The full two-request shape of a Checkmk site: the configuration collection is read first and indexed, then the monitoring query streams every host with its mk_inventory tree attached. Proves the three cases that matter and that a real site always mixes. web01.example.com is fully inventoried, so its MAC comes from hardware.nwadapter, its serial and chassis from hardware.system, its OS from software.os, and two packages from software.packages; its alias is free text and must NOT become a hostname. db01 has never produced an inventory, so its only interface is built from the address Checkmk polls, and its alias IS hostname-shaped and must become a second name. staged01 exists in the configuration and not in the monitoring core -- a host added in the Setup whose changes were never activated -- and is imported from the configuration alone rather than dropped. Payload structure is taken from Checkmk 2.3 source: the collection envelope from constructors.collection_object/domain_object, the configuration extensions from host_config.serialize_host, the monitoring extensions from host._host_object (the raw Livestatus column dict), and the inventory tree from the SDRawTree TypedDict in structured_data.py with the capitalized on-disk reserved keys. Every key name is confirmed against the display hints in inv_hints.py. All data is synthetic.",
